invariant: INV-16
file: rsa_sign.c
catches: test/lint-wide-multiply.sh
reason: mont_mul picks t or t - m with an if instead of a mask, so whether
  a Montgomery product needed its final subtract -- a fact about a secret
  intermediate of the private exponentiation -- decides which path runs.
  The multiply tokens see nothing. The branch count does: every clang spec
  emits more conditional branches in rsa_sign.c than its ceiling records
  (https://github.com/c4milo/chapulin/issues/141).

--- old
    memcpy(o, t, k * sizeof(uint32_t));
    sub_masked(o, m, k, ~mask_of_bit(below(t, m, k, t[k])));
--- new
    memcpy(o, t, k * sizeof(uint32_t));
    if (below(t, m, k, t[k]) == 0) {
        sub_masked(o, m, k, UINT32_MAX);
    }
